course: dictionary
lesson: 8291
title: Risk and the chance of harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A risk is the chance that something bad, like getting hurt or losing something, may happen. «Research suggests time outdoors in daylight lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» The sentence tells you that playing outside makes a bad thing less likely, so risk means the chance of harm.
explain: Risk can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a risk is a thing or situation that could cause harm, such as a wet floor. As a verb, to risk something means to do something that could lead to losing or harming it. «I will risk my new coat by playing in the mud» means the coat might get ruined.
explain: Some risks are worth taking, like trying something new. Others are not worth the risk, like a dare near a busy road or deep water. To take a risk means to do something even though it may go wrong, so think first about how big the risk is and how to lower it.
fact: Risk means the chance that something bad may happen.
fact: «At risk» means in danger of being harmed.
fact: «Take a risk» means do something even though it may go wrong.
fact: A risk assessment is a check made before a school trip to find the dangers and reduce them.
fact: A bet is money risked on something happening; if you lose, you lose your money.
exercise: «Research suggests time outdoors lowers the risk of children becoming short-sighted.» What does risk mean here? | *The chance that something bad may happen | A kind of outdoor game | A place where children play | The hours spent in daylight
exercise: Ella says, «Dinnae worry, I'll take a risk and try the new slide.» What does take a risk mean? | To run away from the slide | To count the steps up the slide | *To do something even though it may go wrong | To keep a safe distance from the slide
exercise: Sam says, «I will risk my new coat by playing in the mud.» What does risk mean here? | To buy a new coat | To hang the coat up | *To do something that could harm the coat | To wash the coat
test: Wearing a helmet when cycling does what to the risk of hurting your head? | Does nothing at all | Makes it into a bet | Raises it | *Lowers it
test: Which of these is not worth the risk? | Trying a new food | Learning a new game | *Running across a busy road without looking | Reading a new book
exam: A risk assessment is | A type of bet | A party for the class | *A check made before a trip to find possible dangers | A thing you eat on a picnic
